HST Office: VBA projects are written with the records real Office files have.

The owner's test of the first forms in real Office: Excel "The ActiveX Designer's Type information
does not match what was saved", Word "Could not open macro storage". Compared with Office-made files
and MS-OVBA:
- MS Forms is a REFERENCECONTROL (2.3.5: the designer's type library MUST be referenced so), not a
  REFERENCEREGISTERED.
- A Word project has the document module ThisDocument and a reference to Normal.
- A form's caption is also in the f stream as UTF-16 and it has a ShapeCookie.
Whether Office accepts the result is not known yet: no Office here.

